   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## kubakub · versions\n\nMany versions of one facade from one queue.\n\n1. **scene render** makes the clay view of the 3D file, **regions from id renders** the regions (roof, wall,\n   windows ...), the **plan** says what every version has in common.\n2. In **kubakub versions** write the sheet: `[look]` whole-facade looks, `[region windows]` ideas for some\n   regions, `[rotate a | b | c]` ideas that move on by one region per version, `[lora]` name : strength : words,\n   `[reference]` style images, `[set denoise]`, `[seed]`. One option per line.\n3. Queue with **quality = draft**: a numbered contact sheet, a few seconds per version.\n   mode *rotate* = version n takes option n of every list, *combine* = every combination, *one by one* = one\n   change at a time.\n4. The drafts are in `output/kubakub/versions`, named after what they are made of. Copy the ones you like into\n   a folder of your own, paste its path into **picks_folder**, set **quality = final**, queue: those pictures at\n   the full canvas size with full-size detail (`final_denoise`: higher = more new detail), saved to\n   `output/kubakub/versions/final`. Or write their numbers from the contact sheet into **pick** (`2, 5`).\n\nChanging one line re-renders only the versions that use it. The report lists every version's rules: paste them\ninto a region plan to keep working on one version by hand.\n\n**You need:** a scene file with a camera (node 1), Blender 4.x, Flux 2 Klein 4B (nodes 10-12).\n"
   ],
   "title": "read me"
  }
 ],
